// FIXED — the forward-edge ordering hole (2026-08-20 audit,
// design/activation_state.md; found via the dyncall_seed_backedge
// fixture regressing under the loud-degrade Err). Kernel definition
// order was REVERSED DECLARATION ORDER as a callees-first
// approximation, which breaks on SIBLING discovery: the root
// references g before f (the shielding select's arm), so discovery
// records [g, f], the reversal defined f FIRST, f's g-call found no
// SiteLayout, and the old silent-0 fallback ran g's activations
// below f's recursion with NO interior memory. Fixed by TOPOLOGICAL
// definition order over the recorded static call edges (emit/jit.rs);
// emit_site_block now Errs loudly instead of passing 0.
//
// TRACE HISTORY: at fix time the ruled trace was [101,1,1,1] (the
// interp's retained instance rode g's held guard verdict over the
// bottomed m at epochs 3-4, pre-fix jit [101,1]). THE
// CONSULTED-GUARD RULE (Eric, same day — a consulted guard whose
// channel is bottom makes the selection undecidable; no held-verdict
// ride) re-blessed it to [101, 1] on BOTH engines: epochs 3-4 bottom
// because g's consulted guard channel is bottom, however sound the
// scrutinee fire. The pin now guards the ORDERING (g defines first,
// f carves real blocks — de-fuse would show as a FuseExpect drift in
// dyncall_seed_backedge) and the consulted-bottom trace.
{let x = array::iter([i64:1, i64:2, i64:0, i64:0]); let m = x / x / i64:3; let g = |k: i64| -> i64 select k - k {i64:0 if m == i64:0 => i64:1, _ => i64:2}; let rec f = |n: i64| -> i64 select n {i64:0 => g(n), _ => f(n - i64:1) + i64:0}; select x {i64:1 => g(i64:5), _ => i64:0} * i64:100 + f(x - x + i64:1)}
